    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d653">

                <pb facs="0908" n="794" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg794"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/426: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-10T10:00:00-06:00">February 10, 1931—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>32. My telegram No. 25, February 3, 10 a.m.<anchor n="14c" xml:id="d653-f1"/>
                    Honduran Congress after third and final reading and some discussion ratified
                    yesterday, by unanimous vote and without reservations, the Honduran Nicaraguan
                    boundary protocol.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Managua.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
